  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="timestamp"><strong>Last updated:</strong> February 26, 2026</p>

  <h2>Your Privacy Matters</h2>
  <p>
    HomeClaw is designed with your privacy as the top priority. Your smart home data stays on your Mac.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing.</strong> We don't collect, store, or transmit any of your HomeKit data or personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>How the App Works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Local Processing</strong>: All HomeKit communication happens directly on your Mac via Apple's HomeKit framework</li>
    <li><strong>No Servers</strong>: Your home data never leaves your device. HomeClaw communicates over a local Unix domain socket only</li>
    <li><strong>No Tracking</strong>: We don't track your usage or collect analytics</li>
    <li><strong>No Accounts</strong>: No sign-up required, no email addresses collected</li>
    <li><strong>No Network Access</strong>: HomeClaw does not make any network requests. All communication is local</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>HomeKit Access</h2>
  <p>When you grant HomeClaw access to your HomeKit data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The app reads your home layout, rooms, accessories, and scenes locally</li>
    <li>Commands to control accessories are sent directly to HomeKit on your Mac</li>
    <li>We cannot and do not upload your home data anywhere</li>
    <li>Your HomeKit access can be revoked at any time in System Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; HomeKit</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third-Party Integrations</h2>
  <p>
    HomeClaw provides a CLI tool and MCP server that allow AI assistants (like Claude) to interact with your HomeKit
    accessories. These integrations:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Communicate only over a local Unix domain socket on your Mac</li>
    <li>Do not send your home data to any external service</li>
    <li>Are entirely optional and can be disabled</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about privacy, contact us at:
    <a href="mailto:homeclaw@omarknows.app">homeclaw@omarknows.app</a>
  </p>
</MarkdownPage>
